        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat: add GitHub Codespaces provider",
        "body": "Closes https://github.com/openclaw/crabbox/issues/348\n\n## Summary\n\nAdds a direct GitHub Codespaces Linux SSH-lease provider with aliases `codespaces` and `gh-codespaces`.\n\n- Creates claim-owned GitHub Codespaces through the GitHub REST API and local `gh` authentication.\n- Uses `gh codespace ssh --config` for Crabbox SSH, rsync, `run`, `ssh`, `status`, `stop`, and cleanup flows.\n- Keeps the provider direct-only; it does not route through the Crabbox coordinator.\n- Adds provider config/flags/env handling, generated metadata, docs, OpenSSH config parsing, lifecycle tests, and guarded live-smoke coverage.\n- Persists durable pre-create recovery intent and binds lifecycle mutations to immutable Codespace, repository, owner, user, API-host, and account identity.\n- Recovers ambiguous creates without adopting pre-existing resources; rejects duplicate claims; serializes slug allocation; and protects Touch, Resolve, Cleanup, and Release with locked compare-and-swap claim updates.\n- Confirms asynchronous deletion by observing absence before removing recovery evidence.\n- Keeps read-only resolution mutation-free and preserves dirty or uncertain resources for operator recovery.\n- Selects host-specific authentication and SSH routing, rejects redirects, and stores generated SSH configuration with private cross-platform permissions.\n\n## Verification\n\nExact candidate: `1e84bfb972afa53013167a5817908e1cf8d8a21c`\n\nLocal gates:\n\n- `go test -race ./...`\n- `go vet ./...`\n- `go build -trimpath -o bin/crabbox ./cmd/crabbox`\n- `go run golang.org/x/tools/cmd/deadcode@v0.45.0 -test ./...` (no findings)\n- Linux, macOS arm64, and Windows amd64 provider cross-compiles\n- provider-matrix, command-doc, docs-link, and docs-site checks\n- Worker format, lint, typecheck, build, and 934 tests\n- GitHub Codespaces smoke contract: 6/6\n- final full and scoped AutoReview passes: no accepted/actionable findings\n\nHosted exact-head gates:\n\n- CI: 7/7 passed — https://github.com/openclaw/crabbox/actions/runs/29084189298\n- Connector E2E: 5/5 passed — https://github.com/openclaw/crabbox/actions/runs/29084189280\n- Blacksmith Testbox: provider `blacksmith-testbox`, lease `tbx_01kx5qe478gfwmjr4hp41f4952`, run https://github.com/openclaw/crabbox/actions/runs/29084828852\n  - asserted the exact candidate before and after the run\n  - clean tree before and after the run\n  - provider race suite\n  - focused durable-claim and conditional-mutation race suite\n  - provider/core vet\n  - Windows amd64 cross-compile\n  - exit 0; one-shot lease stopped and confirmed absent\n\nGitHub reports this candidate MERGEABLE/CLEAN against the current base.\n\n## Remaining live gate\n\nDo not merge yet.\n\nThe implementation and exact-head hosted gates are ready for a maintainer decision, but a credentialed GitHub Codespaces lifecycle remains unproven. The currently authenticated `gh` token has `gist`, `read:org`, `repo`, and `workflow` scopes; `GET /user/codespaces` returns HTTP 403 and explicitly requires the additional `codespace` scope.\n\nBefore merge, authorize that persistent scope expansion and run a redacted exact-head create -> status -> synced run -> SSH -> clean delete proof, including observed final 404 and zero remote/local residue. Separately prove dirty/unpushed stop-and-retain behavior, then decide whether to accept the provider's billing and destructive-cleanup boundary.\n",
        "branch": "feat/github-codespaces-provider",
